%% Figure 5 — Sage Advisory Boundary
%% Diagram Register: docs/publication/DIAGRAM_REGISTER.md, row 5
%% Source Volumes: ADR-002; DS-003 Core Rule; DS-PRD-006
%% Type: Normative | Diagram Standard Class: Trust boundary/security
%% Authoritative Labels: "Sage advises," "Risk Engine — independent authority," "no direct call"
%%
%% Accessibility description (full sentence form, required per DSF-001 §G row 5 / DSF-003 §9.8):
%% This diagram contains no edge — of any style, dashed or solid — from Sage to the Execution Engine
%% or to the Broker Adapter. Sage's only outgoing connection is to Trade Proposal preparation, labeled
%% "Sage advises." The Risk Engine, Execution Engine, and Broker Adapter are enclosed in a separate
%% "Execution Authority Boundary" region that Sage is drawn structurally outside of and has no path
%% into. A proposal reaches the Risk Engine only through the Trade Proposal node, never directly from
%% Sage. Sage's own node label additionally states in text that it has no path to the Execution Engine
%% or Broker Adapter, so the prohibition is legible even without color or line-style perception.
%%
%% HIGH1 repair note (independent-audit finding): the prior version of this diagram represented the
%% prohibition as a dashed "NO DIRECT CALL" arrow from Sage to the Execution Engine and Broker Adapter.
%% Even labeled, a drawn arrow visually represents a path/connection and contradicted the controlling
%% prohibition it was meant to state. Both arrows are removed outright (not restyled) and replaced with
%% a non-path visual mechanism: a boundary subgraph plus an inline textual note on Sage's own node.

graph LR
    Sage["Sage<br/><i>advisory only</i><br/>⛔ no path to Execution Engine or Broker Adapter"]
    Proposal["Trade Proposal"]

    subgraph Boundary["🔒 Execution Authority Boundary — Sage has no path into this region"]
        Risk["Risk Engine<br/><i>independent authority</i>"]
        Exec["Execution Engine"]
        Broker["Broker Adapter"]
        Risk --> Exec
        Exec --> Broker
    end

    Sage -->|"Sage advises"| Proposal
    Proposal -->|"only approved entry into the pipeline"| Risk

    classDef advisory fill:#F4F2EC,color:#0B0B0D,stroke:#3B6EA5,stroke-width:2px;
    classDef authority fill:#F4F2EC,color:#0B0B0D,stroke:#A33A3A,stroke-width:2px;
    classDef neutral fill:#F4F2EC,color:#0B0B0D,stroke:#2A2D33,stroke-width:1px;
    class Sage advisory;
    class Risk authority;
    class Proposal neutral;
    class Exec neutral;
    class Broker neutral;

%% No edge in this file connects Sage to Risk, Exec, or Broker directly — Sage's only edge targets Proposal.
